-- Minimum Wage Law 5747-1987, s 2 (the right to the minimum wage), with the refusals that s 16, s 17
-- and s 18 require. The figures come in as inputs (`the monthly minimum wage`); the published
-- ones are in mw-il32-published-figures.l4 and the capstone entry points in mw-il32-answers.l4.

§ `Section 2(a) — a full-time employee aged 18 or over`

§§ `What the Law does not hold`

-- s 16(a): an employee who has not turned 18 is governed only as the Minister fixes by regulations
-- (with the Labour and Welfare Committee's approval), and s 16(b) lets the regulations set lower
-- rates and other ways of computing. The Law prints no youth rate, no apprentice rate and no age band.
-- src:147 | (א) השר רשאי, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, לקבוע בתקנות הוראות בדבר תחולתו של חוק זה לגבי עובד שטרם מלאו לו 18 שנים; תקנות כאמור יכול שיהיו דרך כלל, לפי סוגי עובדים או לפי סוגי מעסיקים.
-- src:148 | (ב) בתקנות כאמור בסעיף קטן (א) יכול שייקבע שכר מינימום בשיעורים נמוכים מהאמור בחוק זה ויכול שייקבעו בהן כללים לחישוב שכר המינימום השונים מן האמור בחוק זה, לרבות בדבר רכיבי השכר שיובאו בחשבון.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 16(a), (b) (source lines 147-148)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the rate for an employee under 18 is fixed by regulations under section 16 that this model does not hold` MEANS
    REFUSE "the rate for an employee under 18 is fixed by regulations under section 16, which this model does not hold; the Law itself prints none"

-- s 17(a), (b): the Minister may by regulations apply the Law, at lower rates, to employees with
-- physical, mental or intellectual limitations. The consolidation's note names the Minimum Wage
-- (Adjusted Wage for an Employee with a Disability of Reduced Work Capacity) Regulations 5762-2002,
-- which are not deposited.
-- src:151 | (א) הוראות חוק זה יחולו לגבי עובדים שיש להם מגבלות גופניות, נפשיות או שכליות המועסקים במפעלים מוגנים שאוצר המדינה משתתף בתקציבם, בין אם מלאו להם 18 שנים ובין אם לאו, אם קבע כך שר העבודה והרווחה בתקנות, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, דרך כלל או לסוגים; בתקנות כאמור יכול שייקבע שכר מינימום הנמוך מהאמור בחוק זה.
-- src:152 | (ב) השר, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע בתקנות הוראות בדבר תחולתו של חוק זה על עובדים שיש להם מגבלות גופניות, נפשיות או שכליות אף שאינם מועסקים במפעלים מוגנים כאמור בסעיף קטן (א), ויכול שיקבע שכר מינימום לעובדים כאמור או לסוגים מהם, בשיעורים נמוכים מהאמורים בחוק זה.
-- src:153 | [note: פורסמו תקנות שכר מינימום (שכר מותאם לעובד עם מוגבלות בעל יכולת עבודה מופחתת), התשס״ב–2002.]
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 17(a), (b) (source lines 151-153)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the rate for an employee in a class that section 17 regulations may cover is fixed by regulations this model does not hold` MEANS
    REFUSE "the rate for an employee in a class that section 17 regulations may cover is fixed by regulations this model does not hold"

§§ `The minimum wage a full-time employee is entitled to`

-- s 2(a): an employee who has turned 18 and works a full position as customary at the workplace is
-- entitled to pay no lower than the monthly, the daily or the hourly minimum wage, "as the case may be".
-- The case is the basis on which the employee's pay is fixed (the nouns module).
-- "Has turned 18" is read as 18 completed years or more (NOTES.md F9).
-- src:28 | (א) עובד שמלאו לו 18 שנים (להלן – עובד) המועסק במשרה מלאה, כנהוג במקום עבודתו, זכאי לקבל ממעסיקו שכר עבודה שלא יפחת משכר המינימום לחודש, שכר המינימום היומי או שכר המינימום לשעה, הכל לפי הענין.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(a) (source line 28), s 1 (source lines 23-25)
GIVEN `the employee`             IS AN `An employee`
      `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER  @desc the full adult monthly minimum wage on the day asked about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `the employee` `from` `the monthly minimum wage` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the employee`'s `age in completed years` LESS THAN 18
           THEN `the rate for an employee under 18 is fixed by regulations under section 16 that this model does not hold`
           IF `the employee`'s `within a class for which section 17 regulations may fix a lower rate`
           THEN `the rate for an employee in a class that section 17 regulations may cover is fixed by regulations this model does not hold`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the employee`'s `how pay is fixed`
               WHEN `paid by the month` THEN `the monthly minimum wage`
               WHEN `paid by the day`   THEN `the daily minimum wage from` `the monthly minimum wage` `for` (`the employee`'s `the working week`)
               WHEN `paid by the hour`  THEN `the hourly minimum wage from` `the monthly minimum wage`

§ `Section 2(b) — a part-time employee`

§§ `The fraction of a position, from hours (fork F1; ruled by Meng, 2026-10-08, SHRUG)`

-- s 2(b): "an employee employed in a part-time position is entitled to a partial minimum wage that is
-- calculated in proportion to the fraction of his position". The Law does not say how the fraction is
-- measured. By hours, there are two readings:
--   (A) the hours the employee works over the hours of a full position customary at the workplace
--       (s 2(a) "as customary at his workplace");
--   (B) the hours the employee works over the 186 hours of a month that the hourly minimum wage of
--       s 1 implies.
-- They give one answer when the full position customary at the workplace is 186 hours, and different
-- answers otherwise. Default: decline where they differ, answer where they agree. A fraction is capped
-- at 1: an employee who works at least a full position is a full-time employee under s 2(a), and
-- s 2(b) does not raise the minimum above the full figure.
-- src:29 | (ב) עובד המועסק במשרה חלקית זכאי לשכר מינימום חלקי שיחושב יחסית לחלקיות משרתו.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29), s 2(a) (source line 28), s 1 "שכר מינימום לשעה" (source line 25); fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Law does not decide how to measure a part-time position by hours` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law does not decide how to measure the fraction of a part-time position by hours: reading A uses the hours of a full position customary at the workplace, reading B the 186 hours of s 1, and they give different answers here"

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(a), (b); the hours of a full position are not given
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the hours of a full position customary at the workplace are needed and were not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "the fraction of the position needs the hours of a full position customary at the workplace (section 2(a)), and none were given"

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29); fork F1
GIVEN `the hours`   IS A NUMBER
      `the divisor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fraction of a position that` `the hours` `are of a position of` `the divisor` MEANS
    IF `the divisor` AT MOST 0
    THEN REFUSE "a position of no hours has no fraction"
    ELSE IF `the hours` AT LEAST `the divisor` THEN 1 ELSE `the hours` DIVIDED BY `the divisor`

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29); fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the work`    IS AN `Hours of work in a month`
      `the reading` IS A `How the fraction of a position is measured`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fraction of a full position under section 2(b) for` `the work` `read` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `by the hours of a full position customary at the workplace` THEN
        CONSIDER `the work`'s `hours of a full position customary at the workplace in the month`
        WHEN JUST h THEN `the fraction of a position that` (`the work`'s `hours the employee works in the month`) `are of a position of` h
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the hours of a full position customary at the workplace are needed and were not given`
    WHEN `by the 186 hours of a month that section 1 implies` THEN
        `the fraction of a position that` (`the work`'s `hours the employee works in the month`) `are of a position of` `the hours in a month that the hourly minimum wage assumes`
    WHEN `decline where the readings differ` THEN
        CONSIDER `the work`'s `hours of a full position customary at the workplace in the month`
        WHEN JUST h THEN
            IF h EQUALS `the hours in a month that the hourly minimum wage assumes`
            THEN `the fraction of a position that` (`the work`'s `hours the employee works in the month`) `are of a position of` h
            ELSE `the Law does not decide how to measure a part-time position by hours`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Law does not decide how to measure a part-time position by hours`

§§ `The partial minimum wage`

-- A partial minimum wage is the full figure times the fraction. It is defined here for an employee
-- whose pay is fixed by the month. For the daily and hourly bases the text is silent on what a
-- fraction of a position does to the figure (an hourly minimum wage is already per hour), and the
-- row's brief asks only for the monthly figure, so those two decline by name (NOTES.md F10).
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29); s 18(b)(1), (2) (source lines 158-159)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Law does not say what a fraction of a position does to a daily or an hourly minimum wage` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law does not say what a fraction of a position does to a daily or an hourly minimum wage; only the monthly basis is answered"

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29)
GIVEN `the employee`             IS AN `An employee`
      `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction`             IS A NUMBER  @desc the fraction of a full position, greater than 0 and at most 1
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the partial minimum wage under section 2(b) for` `the employee` `from` `the monthly minimum wage` `at the fraction` `the fraction` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the fraction` AT MOST 0 OR `the fraction` GREATER THAN 1
           THEN REFUSE "a part-time position is a fraction greater than 0 and at most 1"
           IF   NOT (`the employee`'s `how pay is fixed` EQUALS `paid by the month`)
           THEN `the Law does not say what a fraction of a position does to a daily or an hourly minimum wage`
           OTHERWISE `the minimum wage under section 2(a) for` `the employee` `from` `the monthly minimum wage` TIMES `the fraction`

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(b) (source line 29); fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the employee`             IS AN `An employee`
      `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the work`                 IS AN `Hours of work in a month`
      `the reading`              IS A `How the fraction of a position is measured`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum wage of a part-time position under section 2(b) for` `the employee` `from` `the monthly minimum wage` `on` `the work` `read` `the reading` MEANS
    `the partial minimum wage under section 2(b) for` `the employee` `from` `the monthly minimum wage` `at the fraction` (`the fraction of a full position under section 2(b) for` `the work` `read` `the reading`)

§ `Section 2(c) — absence from work`

-- s 2(c): "if an employee is absent from work, the minimum wage he is entitled to under subsection (a)
-- shall be reduced in proportion to the time of his absence; but if he is entitled to receive payment
-- for the time of absence by law, an employment contract, a collective agreement, an extension order,
-- another collective arrangement, or by the provisions that bind a provident fund (in this section,
-- the arrangement), the payment shall be as the arrangement provides".
-- The Law does not say whether the time is measured in days or in hours, so the caller supplies the
-- fraction of the working time the employee was absent (NOTES.md F5). Where the arrangement pays,
-- the minimum for the absent time is whatever the arrangement pays, which the caller supplies.
-- src:30 | (ג) נעדר עובד מעבודתו, יקטן שכר המינימום שהוא זכאי לו לפי סעיף קטן (א), בשיעור יחסי לזמן היעדרו, ואולם אם הוא זכאי לקבל תשלום בעד זמן ההיעדרות לפי דין, חוזה עבודה, הסכם קיבוצי, צו הרחבה או הסדר קיבוצי אחר או לפי ההוראות המחייבות קופת גמל (בסעיף זה – ההסדר), יהיה התשלום לפי הוראות ההסדר.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(c) (source line 30)
GIVEN `the minimum wage for the whole period, had there been no absence` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of the working time the employee was absent`        IS A NUMBER
      `the payment the arrangement gives for the absent time`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum wage after an absence, from` `the minimum wage for the whole period, had there been no absence` `with absence of` `the fraction of the working time the employee was absent` `and arrangement payment` `the payment the arrangement gives for the absent time` MEANS
    IF   `the fraction of the working time the employee was absent` LESS THAN 0 OR `the fraction of the working time the employee was absent` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN REFUSE "the fraction of the working time absent is between 0 and 1"
    ELSE `the minimum wage for the whole period, had there been no absence` TIMES (1 MINUS `the fraction of the working time the employee was absent`)
         PLUS (CONSIDER `the payment the arrangement gives for the absent time`
               WHEN JUST p THEN p
               WHEN NOTHING THEN 0)
